          "Lead with young renter economic security: housing affordability, rental protections, wage growth, and access to childcare and healthcare are the material daily concerns of a 33.7-year-old, 39.5% renter constituency at $50,273 income. Policy specificity on these issues is far more electorally relevant than abstract messaging.",
          "Disaggregate the diverse constituency and demonstrate specific attention to each community: the Black community (22.78%), Hispanic community (17.89%), and white working-class majority each have distinct needs around economic mobility, language access, and community investment. Treating diversity as a single category is governance malpractice in a district this heterogeneous.",
          "Do not assume the unopposed margin is durable — if a credible challenger emerges with a coherent economic message and visible relationships across multiple demographic communities, the absence of demonstrated incumbent engagement becomes an exploitable vulnerability. Invest in constituent relationship-building now, while no active opposition exists."
