          "Avoid treating 51% as a majority: in a 51-49 seat, the incumbent's coalition is held by the perception of competence and constituent service, not by partisan loyalty or demographic inevitability — any candidate who consolidates only their base without addressing the opposition's concrete concerns is vulnerable to a well-resourced, issue-focused challenger."
