          { name: "Treating Low Educational Attainment as a Proxy for Ignorance or Disengagement", tag: "avoid", why: "The 21% college attainment reflects a working-class and agricultural constituency, not a constituency incapable of sophisticated judgment about economic policy or governance quality. Candidates who campaign down to this demographic — using simplistic messaging, avoiding policy specificity, or defaulting to cultural grievance — insult the intelligence of homeowners who have successfully managed modest incomes and asset-holding across decades. This constituency evaluates on concrete results and clear answers to material concerns." },
          { name: "Assuming Rural Service Issues Will Resolve Themselves Without Legislative Attention", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district with 83.9% homeownership, rural service reliability — hospital access, broadband, water infrastructure, emergency response — is not a peripheral concern but a direct quality-of-life issue for most households. A representative who fails to engage these material infrastructure and service concerns, or who assumes that private markets will resolve rural service gaps, will find opposition mobilizing around the gap between constituent need and legislative response. These are concrete governance issues that demand specific legislative action and constituent attention." }
