          "Engage the Choctaw Nation as a governing partner, not a special interest—the Nation is the largest employer in Bryan County and a civic institution on par with state government; fluency on tribal healthcare access, economic development, and state-tribal partnership is a basic prerequisite for representing this district.",
          "Do not assume the 33% opposition is inert; it likely represents a combination of working-class voters frustrated by economic stagnation, mobilized tribal community members, and younger renters evaluating on opportunity—identify which groups comprise the opposition and address their specific concerns rather than assuming they will not consolidate against an inattentive incumbent.",
          "Campaign on material governance outcomes, not partisan messaging; at this income level and education profile, voters evaluate on whether state government is visibly improving wages, housing affordability, healthcare access, and childcare costs—not on abstract ideological positioning."
