          "Investigate and engage any Native American population represented in the ~3-4% demographic gap; without specific data on this community's size, geographic concentration, or electoral behavior, any candidate is operating with incomplete information about a portion of the district's actual constituency.",
          "Build a legislative record or campaign message that directly addresses working-class economic concerns — not abstract conservative positioning, but specific policy commitments on healthcare access, housing affordability, or wage-level job creation that resonate with a $70K median-income constituency.",
          "Do not assume unopposed status indicates electoral safety; 100% of zero votes cast by an opposition party in a low-turnout special election is not the same as 100% of votes cast in a competitive general election. Treat 2026 as genuinely open and build constituent relationships as though the margin is negotiable."
