          { name: "Dismissing or Ignoring the 26% Opposition", tag: "avoid", why: "While 26% is a small opposition in a Republican stronghold, understanding who comprises this constituency—where they live, what their specific concerns are, whether they are renters, younger adults, Hispanic voters, or concentrated in particular neighborhoods—is strategically important for preventing consolidation of a base around an alternative candidate. Governance that ignores the opposition's material concerns, particularly around housing affordability or cost-of-living issues, risks allowing opposition recruitment to succeed among segments that are not inherently partisan but are responsive to specific material grievances." }
