          { name: "Assuming Abstract Conservative Positioning Substitutes for Demonstrated Results", tag: "avoid", why: "At 32.5% college attainment and $91,605 income, HD-57 is an educated, affluent constituency that evaluates policy on evidence and demonstrated outcomes, not ideological positioning. A legislator who relies on abstract conservative rhetoric while delivering ambiguous or absent results on the fiscal management, education quality, and infrastructure maintenance that this district actually cares about is vulnerable to a challenger — including potentially a moderate Republican or independent — who can point to concrete accomplishments. This is not a district where partisan identity is sufficient to hold the seat; governance competence is the necessary condition." }
