          { name: "Complacency About Demographic Stability Masking Vulnerability to Credible Opposition", tag: "avoid", why: "The apparent stability of HD-60 — settled homeowners, high income, college-educated, low renter rate — can create false confidence that the seat is electorally safe without active constituent engagement. A challenger with credible local standing, specific appeal to the 3.34% demographic gap, or a message tailored to younger adults' concerns (healthcare costs, education affordability, economic opportunity) could find substantially more traction than the 76% headline suggests. Mayfield's vulnerability increases directly with any assumption that the seat will hold itself without active work to consolidate homeowner support and build relationship with emerging communities." }
