          { name: "Overestimating Demographic Stability as Political Permanence", tag: "avoid", why: "The demographic profile of HD-73—89.95% white, $70,862 income, low college attainment, low renter rate—is stable and will not shift dramatically in the near term. However, demographic stability does not guarantee political stability; specific policy failures, constituent service lapses, or the emergence of a primary challenger with a more focused local message can erode even a large margin. The 18.7% college attainment rate and working-to-middle-class income profile mean this constituency is not driven by abstract ideology but by practical governance outcomes: does my representative solve local problems? Do they understand my economic concerns? Are they accessible? These are the questions that determine whether a 77% margin stays durable or becomes vulnerable to a motivated primary opponent." }
