          "Monitor the renter-vs.-homeowner split in the district's voting behavior; at 30.8% renter rate in a district this young, renters represent meaningful swing voters, and messaging that appears homeowner-focused or dismissive of renter concerns risks hemorrhaging support among voters who have no equity stake and are evaluating purely on economic and service delivery performance."
