          "Engage the Black community (31%) and Hispanic community (17%) with specific constituent service and community-defined priorities: these two communities together represent nearly half of HD-92, and a 59-41 result suggests that Black and Latino voters are not yet fully mobilized or are being taken for granted; a challenger or primary opponent who invests in genuine constituent attention could reveal significant opportunity in these communities.",
          "Treat working-class economic mobility as the core message: with only 29.6% college attainment and $65,149 income, this district evaluates on whether jobs are available, whether they pay enough to cover housing, and whether healthcare is affordable — not on cultural signaling or abstract policy positioning; any candidate who centers material economic security will outperform one oriented toward college-educated constituencies.",
