          "Develop a renter-centered housing and affordability agenda: rent stabilization, tenant protections, first-time homebuyer support, and childcare access are the material concerns of a 32.1-year-old, 45.4%-renter constituency; generic Democratic messaging on housing will not compete with a challenger who offers specific, implementable solutions to monthly cost-of-living pressure.",
          "Engage the Black community (38%) and white community (39%) as distinct constituencies with specific constituent service records: both communities include working-class families for whom job quality, healthcare access, and educational opportunity are the driving concerns; demonstrate tangible legislative wins for each community rather than assuming demographic alignment guarantees loyalty.",
          "Monitor the 15.65% Hispanic population actively for signs of economic pressure or unmet constituent needs; in a district this racially balanced, any community that concludes the incumbent is not delivering can become the swing group in a primary challenge or general election, so constituent service and visibility must extend explicitly to this population."
