          { name: "Rural Healthcare Access as Secondary Rather Than Primary", tag: "avoid", why: "While rural healthcare access is a legitimate concern in exurban Indiana, IN-SD-35's median age of 34.6 and renter rate of 41.6% suggest the dominant material concerns for most constituency members are housing affordability, wage quality, and childcare access rather than healthcare service geography. Any candidate who leads on rural hospital preservation or healthcare access without also engaging the renter affordability and job-quality concerns that directly affect younger families' economic security is misdiagnosing what drives the 43% opposition in this district; healthcare is important but not the primary material issue for a constituency whose median household income places healthcare costs in competition with housing and childcare." }
