          "Do not treat a 57-43 margin as safe in a district with 41.6% renters, a 34.6-year median age, and below-average college attainment; this is a working-class constituency evaluating on material delivery, not inherited partisan identity, and any incumbent who consolidates only the homeowner base while neglecting renter economic anxiety will find the margin compressed in a competitive cycle."
