          "Engage the 13.48% Asian and 8.4% Hispanic communities with active constituent service and policy responsiveness; these are not marginal populations in a 62-38 district, and their economic and social concerns around education, housing, and healthcare access deserve legislative attention rather than tokenism.",
          "Do not treat a 62% margin as a permanent floor: suburban voters in the 35.6-year median age and 38.2% renter range have demonstrated capacity to shift parties when they conclude government is not delivering economic security. Active constituent service and demonstrated results on schools, housing affordability, and public safety are what sustain this seat across cycles.",
          "Recognize that the 38% opposition is large enough to represent a coherent constituency with specific governance concerns—young families frustrated with school funding, renters concerned about housing costs, and minority communities evaluating on whether they are receiving equitable service. Understanding what drives that 38% is as important as consolidating the 62%."
