          { name: "Conflating Homeowner Interests with District Interests", tag: "avoid", why: "The 79% homeownership implied by the renter rate means the homeowner majority is substantial and politically important; but it also means that one-fifth of the district has different economic concerns and can become a vulnerability if neglected. A representative whose legislative record and messaging center only on homeowner concerns — property tax cuts, school funding for affluent districts, road infrastructure for commuters — and who dismisses renter concerns as socialist or outside state scope is actively creating space for a challenger who can credibly claim to represent the full district. At 76%, this is not immediately fatal, but it is strategically reckless." }
