          "Address the $62,397 median income directly: In a district where household economic security is constrained, a legislative agenda focused on cost-of-living pressures—property tax management, healthcare affordability, rural service delivery, and workforce development for non-college pathways—is both materially responsive and politically durable.",
          "Recognize the 27.2% renter constituency as a distinct group: While homeowners dominate, renters in rural districts face specific constraints around housing stability and affordability; targeted attention to this group demonstrates governance that reaches beyond the default homeowner base and builds a broader coalition.",
          "Monitor demographic change as a long-term strategic signal: The 91.34% white, 39.5-year-old profile and 3.23% Hispanic population together suggest a demographically static district—but the 27.2% renter rate and rural economic pressure may accelerate out-migration or in-migration patterns over the next decade; staying attentive to these early signals prevents strategic surprise."
